==Icelandic==

===Verb===
{{is-verb}}

# to [[lose]] (objects)

====Derived terms====
* [[týna niður|týna [einhverju] niður]] (to forget [something] which was previously known, specifically something which had been learnt)
*: ''Ég tala ekki mikla [[franska|frönsku]], og ég er búin að '''týna niður''' því litla sem ég kunni.''
*:: I don't speak much French, and I've '''forgotten''' what little I knew.
* [[týna lífi]] (to [[die]]- most often used for fatalities occurring in [[warfare]] or by accident)

====Usage notes====
* The [[imperative]] mood of the verb '''''týna''''' (''[[týndu]]'') is most often used with a negative (the word ''[[ekki#Icelandic|ekki]]'').
* It's not possible to "lose" insubstantial things like ''[[von]]'' ("[[hope]]") ''[[gleði]]'' ("[[joy]]"). For that the word ''[[missa]]'' would rather be used. (the exception to this is the phrase ''[[týna lífi|'''týna''' lífi]]'' meaning literally "to lose [one's] life" that is "to [[die]]").

